    <section class="phase-section">
        <h2>HTTP Status vs API Response Code</h2>

        <p>
            During testing, I observed that some API responses
            returned HTTP status 200 while the JSON response body
            contained a different responseCode.
        </p>

        <div class="cards-container">

            <div class="info-card">
                <h3>HTTP Status Code</h3>
                <p>
                    Indicates the HTTP-level result
                    of the request.
                </p>
            </div>

            <div class="info-card">
                <h3>API Response Code</h3>
                <p>
                    A value returned inside the JSON body
                    to describe the application's result.
                </p>
            </div>

            <div class="info-card">
                <h3>Practical Example</h3>
                <p>
                    In API-TC-004, the HTTP status was 200,
                    while the JSON responseCode was 400
                    because a required parameter was missing.
                </p>
            </div>

        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="phase-section">
        <h2>Test Assertion Improvement</h2>

        <p>
            While testing product search, an initial assertion
            checked whether every returned product name
            contained the search keyword.
        </p>

        <p>
            Further investigation showed that some relevant
            products matched through their category information,
            such as Tops &amp; Shirts, rather than their name.
        </p>

        <p>
            I improved the assertion to consider matching
            product names or categories.
            The updated assertions passed.
        </p>

        <p>
            This was treated as a test assertion improvement,
            not a confirmed API defect.
        </p>
    </section>

